# Frontend rules (Next.js)

Mirrors `frontend/CLAUDE.md`. Keep both in sync (parity table in root `CLAUDE.md`).
The Next.js client landed in slice **S-002** (Wave 3). Current build state lives in `README.md` +
the latest slice, not here.

## Boundary

The web client is **UI only**. It calls FastAPI `/v1` and nothing else. No business logic, no
pricing math, no direct LLM/Razorpay/Supabase-DB calls in route handlers. Supabase client SDK is
used **only** for the auth session (get JWT); every data operation goes through FastAPI.

## Rendering

- Server Components by default (dashboard list, proposal detail shell).
- `"use client"` only for: the split editor, forms, checkout redirect, hooks, localStorage.

## Structure

- Pages: `src/app/**/page.tsx`
- Components: `src/components/`
- API client: `src/lib/api.ts` — one place. Attaches `Authorization: Bearer <supabase JWT>`. Do not scatter `fetch`.

## Proposal editor (spec §3, §15)

- Split UI: PDF-like **preview** (left/main) + **section forms** (right rail / full-screen on mobile).
- Bind forms to the same fields as the preview. `PATCH` sends allowlisted fields only.
- **No JSON editor. No "Export JSON" / "Copy source" control. Ever.**
- Free plan: watermark visible on preview **and** in the downloaded PDF; no follow-up-email copy button.
- Changing a price field is a normal `PATCH` — it must not trigger a regenerate.

## Auth

Session + JWT from the Supabase client SDK. `api.ts` attaches the bearer token. On `401`, send the
user back through Supabase sign-in (email verified + Google only).

## UI

- Tailwind. AI-generated copy is editable text, presented as a draft the user owns.
- Reuse primitives; JSDoc on components (purpose, props, state).

## Local commits

Never commit on `main` — feature branch + PR. `.githooks/pre-commit` enforces this.

## Testing

See the "Testing" section of `frontend/CLAUDE.md` (mirrors `.cursor/rules/testing.mdc`).
Jest + RTL, colocated under `__tests__/`. Test behavior, not implementation. Assert the
"no Export JSON" and "watermark on free" invariants where relevant.
